  "fanTake": "Well, that was humbling in the way only a 35-6 road loss can be. The Patriots mustered exactly two field goals while Jacksonville's offense—led by a Trevor Lawrence who looked genuinely comfortable—found the end zone five times. Drake Maye's three turnovers and the offense's -0.25 EPA/play tells you everything: we couldn't move the ball, and when we did manage to reach Jacksonville's red zone four times, we scored zero touchdowns. The defense allowed 0.23 EPA/play and got gashed on third down (Jacksonville converted 8 of 12 to our 4 of 12), so there wasn't much covering for an offense that looked thoroughly unacceptable.",
